{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://pagentos.local/schemas/device-protocol.schema.json",
  "title": "Personal Agent OS device protocol v1",
  "oneOf": [
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/hello" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/challenge" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/auth" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/welcome" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/heartbeat" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/heartbeat_ack" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/command" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/command_ack" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/cancel" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/error" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/voice_sideband" }
  ],
  "$defs": {
    "errorObject": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["class", "message"],
      "properties": {
        "class": {
          "enum": [
            "validation_error",
            "auth_error",
            "device_offline",
            "capability_missing",
            "dependency_unavailable",
            "provider_rate_limited",
            "provider_error",
            "ui_target_not_found",
            "ui_state_changed",
            "timeout",
            "command_expired",
            "cancelled",
            "retry_exhausted",
            "artifact_render_error",
            "voice_provider_error",
            "security_scope_error",
            "browser_lifecycle_violation",
            "focus_mismatch",
            "permission_denied",
            "postcondition_failed",
            "unsupported_format",
            "not_found",
            "internal_bug"
          ]
        },
        "message": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 2000 },
        "retryable": { "type": "boolean" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "hello": {
      "$comment": "ADR-0118 + addendum. An EMITTER sends only the properties declared here (additionalProperties false). A RECEIVER must ignore undeclared top-level properties of hello and validate every declared one strictly: hello is how a build announces itself, and refusing it refuses the whole connection, so a newer agent must still handshake with an older Cloud Core. build_id / source_revision are optional so an agent built before ADR-0118 still handshakes.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "protocol_version", "device_id", "software_version", "capabilities"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "hello" },
        "protocol_version": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
        "device_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
        "software_version": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 64 },
        "build_id": { "type": ["string", "null"], "maxLength": 64 },
        "source_revision": { "type": ["string", "null"], "maxLength": 64 },
        "capabilities": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_.]{1,63}$" },
          "maxItems": 128
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "challenge": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "nonce"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "challenge" },
        "nonce": { "type": "string", "contentEncoding": "base64", "minLength": 16, "maxLength": 128 }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "auth": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "signature"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "auth" },
        "signature": { "type": "string", "contentEncoding": "base64", "maxLength": 512 }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "welcome": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "session_id", "heartbeat_interval_s"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "welcome" },
        "session_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
        "heartbeat_interval_s": { "type": "number", "exclusiveMinimum": 0, "maximum": 300 }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "heartbeat": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "seq"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "heartbeat" },
        "seq": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
        "status": { "$ref": "#/$defs/deviceStatus" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "deviceStatus": {
      "$comment": "M18.3 (DEVICE_PROTOCOL.md §6g): OPTIONAL and additive; protocol_version stays 1. What the owner-session companion currently sees, attached by the Device Service when the companion answers desktop.activity_status within 1.5 s. Absent means 'not known', never 'nothing is happening': no companion connected, a slow companion, or an agent older than this field all produce a heartbeat without it, and presence/liveness never depend on it. The key set is CLOSED (additionalProperties false) and the Device Service projects onto exactly these keys before sending, so a newer companion cannot make a heartbeat fail validation. It carries no key, character, pointer position, window title or application name: input_idle_s is derived from one tick count, display_state is what the OS broadcast, and the alarm fields are the agent's own state.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "input_idle_s": { "type": ["number", "null"], "minimum": 0 },
        "display_state": { "enum": ["unknown", "off", "on", "dimmed"] },
        "display_observed_at": { "type": ["string", "null"], "format": "date-time" },
        "alarm_ringing": { "type": "boolean" },
        "ringing_alarm_id": { "type": ["string", "null"], "maxLength": 128 },
        "armed_alarms": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
        "next_alarm_at": { "type": ["string", "null"], "format": "date-time" },
        "local_alarm_fired": {
          "$comment": "B13 requirement 282: the ids this device rang on its OWN fallback since the last report, drained when reported. Cloud Core diffs it against the previous report and reconciles, which is what makes requirement 283 (no second ring from the cloud) enforceable: without the id the cloud knows a fallback rang but not WHICH alarm, so it cannot tell that the one it is about to fire has already woken the owner. Absent means 'nothing rang locally', which is also what an older agent sends.",
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 128 },
          "maxItems": 32
        },
        "local_alarm_snoozed": {
          "$comment": "B47 (B13 requirement 259's local trigger; packages/protocol/device-voice.json local_snooze): alarms this device snoozed on its OWN while the Cloud Core was unreachable, drained when reported. 'until' is the instant the device will ring again; the cloud adopts it rather than re-deriving it from the moment the report arrived. Absent means nothing was snoozed locally.",
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": ["alarm_id", "until"],
            "properties": {
              "alarm_id": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 128 },
              "until": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "maxItems": 32
        },
        "voice": {
          "$comment": "B47 (rows 250-252; packages/protocol/device-voice.json heartbeat): the device voice service's compact health. States, flags, a counter and an error CLASS - never a transcript, a phrase, a device name or audio. 'disabled' is what a companion without voice reports.",
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["state", "indicator", "mode", "listening", "mic_muted", "cloud_connected", "restarts", "last_error"],
          "properties": {
            "state": { "enum": ["disabled", "starting", "running", "offline", "backoff", "stopped"] },
            "indicator": { "enum": ["off", "muted", "listening", "wake_word", "push_to_talk", "sending"] },
            "mode": { "enum": ["continuous", "wake_word", "push_to_talk"] },
            "listening": { "type": "boolean" },
            "mic_muted": { "type": ["boolean", "null"] },
            "cloud_connected": { "type": "boolean" },
            "restarts": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
            "last_error": { "type": ["string", "null"], "maxLength": 128 }
            },
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "camera": {
          "$comment": "B48 (DEVICE_PROTOCOL.md §6p): the device camera's own state. mode is the owner's choice as the device holds it (off after every start); state is what the camera is doing - 'blocked' when Windows' permission or the device-local switch denies it, 'vetoed' when the owner closed it from the tray on this device. error is a short token, never free text. Absent on a companion without a camera path.",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "mode": { "enum": ["off", "periodic", "continuous"] },
            "state": { "enum": ["off", "idle", "capturing", "blocked", "unavailable", "busy", "vetoed", "error"] },
            "interval_s": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 3600 },
            "indicator": { "enum": ["hidden", "armed", "open"] },
            "last_check_at": { "type": ["string", "null"], "format": "date-time" },
            "error": { "type": ["string", "null"], "maxLength": 64 }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "presence": {
          "$comment": "B48 (DEVICE_PROTOCOL.md §6p): the device-local presence provider's latest observation - exactly the seven structured fields of M18_HOLOGRAPHIC_CORE_SPEC.md §2, source 'camera', or null. A DERIVED signal: the frames it came from were analysed in memory on the device and never stored or sent. Cloud Core screens it with the same boundary as every other observation.",
          "type": ["object", "null"],
          "required": ["person_present", "presence_confidence", "activity_level", "posture", "awake_state", "observed_at", "source"],
          "properties": {
            "person_present": { "type": "boolean" },
            "presence_confidence": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1 },
            "activity_level": { "enum": ["none", "low", "medium", "high"] },
            "posture": { "enum": ["unknown", "upright", "resting"] },
            "awake_state": { "enum": ["awake", "resting", "uncertain"] },
            "observed_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
            "source": { "const": "camera" }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "notify_actions": {
          "$comment": "B11-toast (row 370; packages/protocol/desktop-notify.json action_event): toast buttons the owner pressed, each carried in up to 3 consecutive reports and recorded once by the Cloud Core (keyed on notification_id, action_id and pressed_at). action_id is verbatim from the desktop.notify request that raised the toast - the Cloud Core's own closed vocabulary. Absent on a companion without the Windows toast surface.",
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": ["notification_id", "action_id", "pressed_at"],
            "properties": {
              "notification_id": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 64 },
              "action_id": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z0-9_]{1,32}$" },
              "pressed_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "maxItems": 16
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "heartbeat_ack": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "seq"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "heartbeat_ack" },
        "seq": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "command": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "command"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "command" },
        "command": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["command_id", "idempotency_key", "capability", "payload", "expires_at", "trace_id"],
          "properties": {
            "command_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
            "idempotency_key": { "type": "string", "minLength": 8, "maxLength": 128 },
            "capability": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_.]{1,63}$" },
            "payload": { "type": "object" },
            "expires_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
            "trace_id": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 128 }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "command_ack": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "command_id", "status"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "command_ack" },
        "command_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
        "status": { "enum": ["accepted", "running", "succeeded", "failed"] },
        "result": { "type": ["object", "null"] },
        "error": {
          "anyOf": [{ "$ref": "#/$defs/errorObject" }, { "type": "null" }]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "cancel": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "command_id"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "cancel" },
        "command_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "error"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "error" },
        "command_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
        "error": { "$ref": "#/$defs/errorObject" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "voice_sideband": {
      "$comment": "M12 (ADR-0039): broker -> agent, additive. A realtime-voice sideband push for the owner-session companion. The Device Service forwards it opaquely over the local IPC and never acts on it; no acknowledgement, no idempotency, no audit semantics of the command path apply. Bounded to 16 KiB serialized. Receivers that predate this frame answer it with a validation_error frame, which the broker logs and ignores.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["type", "session_id", "event", "payload"],
      "properties": {
        "type": { "const": "voice_sideband" },
        "session_id": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
        "event": {
          "enum": ["plan_changed", "tool_progress", "tool_completed", "narration_cursor", "say", "leg_closed"]
        },
        "payload": { "type": "object" },
        "at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  }
}
